  m_text: "Blackjack, formerly also Black Jack and Vingt-Un, is the American member
    of a global family of banking games known as Twenty-One, whose relatives include
    the British game of Pontoon and the European game, Vingt-et-Un.[1] \n\nIt is
    a comparing card game between one or more players and a dealer, where each player
    in turn competes against the dealer. Players do not compete against each other.
    It is played with one or more decks of 52 cards, and is the most widely played
    casino banking game in the world. inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules
    and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules
    and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules
    and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules and inforules
    and inforules and inforules and"
